From: Simon Polack <spolack+git@mailbox.org>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ipv4: inet_gso_segment: the segment skb lines two ahead

EXPERIMENTAL, showcase only, not for merging: it needs proper testing.
It changes generic kernel code but was only measured with the octeon_pip
driver of #26060.
The build does not apply it: it sits in target/linux/octeon/experimental/.

The prefetch of the next segment's header line (patch 081) itself loaded
the next segment's skb lines cold (0.9 L1 misses per packet on the P2
image, 38 % at the next pointer, 54 % at head). Prefetch the skb lines
of the segment after the next, so that every line the prefetch
computation reads was prefetched an iteration ago.

Measured on an EdgeRouter 4 (CN7030, 4 cores), octeon3 subtarget (CN63XXP1
off), octeon_pip driver, one boot per image, 64-byte single-flow floods
in kpps, on 2026-10-21.
Target: inet_gso_segment(): 0.92 -> 0.24 L1 misses per packet (flood1).
Step P4 -> P5 (083-087 together, with 085, which was dropped): flood1
+3.0 %, fw4 NAT +2.3 %, fw4+flowtable +2.8 %.
This patch, extrapolated from its share of the misses the step removed (0.68 of 1.68):
flood1 ~+1.2 %, fw4 NAT ~+0.9 %, fw4+flowtable ~+1.1 %. Depends on 081.
These gains are on top of an unpatched octeon3 kernel; the full set and the
split gain (up to +15 %) are in target/linux/octeon/experimental/README.md.

Signed-off-by: Simon Polack <spolack+git@mailbox.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/net/ipv4/af_inet.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/af_inet.c
@@ -1410,10 +1410,20 @@ struct sk_buff *inet_gso_segment(struct
 
 	skb = segs;
 	do {
-		/* The next segment's header line and shared info while this one is done */
+		/*
+		 * The next segment's header line and shared info while this
+		 * one is done, and the skb lines of the one after it: every
+		 * line read here was prefetched an iteration ago
+		 */
 		if (skb->next) {
-			prefetch(skb_mac_header(skb->next) + nhoff);
-			prefetch(skb_shinfo(skb->next));
+			struct sk_buff *n1 = skb->next, *n2 = n1->next;
+
+			prefetch(skb_mac_header(n1) + nhoff);
+			prefetch(skb_shinfo(n1));
+			if (n2) {
+				prefetch(n2);
+				prefetch(&n2->head);
+			}
 		}
 		iph = (struct iphdr *)(skb_mac_header(skb) + nhoff);
 		if (udpfrag) {
